y has a custom design system or style guide that would make this a violation.\n\nLooking at the padding requirements, PropertyDetail.tsx has slightly different padding values than the standard `p-6 max-sm:p-3` — it uses `px-6 max-sm:px-3 py-6` for the main content, though the loading and error states do match the standard. This is close enough to be acceptable.\n\nNow checking the layout-agnostic component requirement...\n\ncomponents are using `py-6 border-b` patterns for section spacing, which technically adds padding to the component root, but it's a consistent pattern throughout the page layout so it seems acceptable.\n\nI'm noticing a discrepancy with PropertyInfo — the test spec expects it to display property type, guest count, bedrooms, beds, and bathrooms with icons, but PropertyInfo.tsx only shows check-in and check-out times. Those property details are actually displayed in PropertyHeader.tsx instead. Let me verify what PropertyInfo is actually rendering versus what the spec requires. So the test spec actually expects PropertyInfo to display property type, guest count, bedroom/bed/bathroom details with icons, plus check-in/check-out times—but the current code only shows the timing information. The property details are split into PropertyHeader instead, which violates the directive to ensure components match their test spec requirements. So there's a clear mismatch here—PropertyInfo should contain the property type, room counts, and check-in/check-out details based on the test spec, but currently it only shows the timing information while PropertyHeader has the property details. This violates the requirement to ensure test entries are satisfied by the actual component code. I need to consolidate these details into PropertyInfo where the tests expect them. alt` attributes but the test expects `fetch` calls to use query parameters - let me verify the actual implementation.\n\nSo I've identified three clear violations: PropertyInfo is missing several required 