ages mid-test, and both the single image and no images tests modify the same property constant. If these run in parallel, they could interfere with each other, so they need to be wrapped in `test.describe.serial`. That's a violation.\n\nLet me map out all the directive violations I've found across the test files so far, starting with the missing `beforeAll` with `truncateAndSeed` that should be in every test file. So every single test file is missing the required `beforeAll` hook with `truncateAndSeed` — property-detail is calling a different function instead, and the other five have nothing at all. For the booking-card issue, the tests are trying to interact with date inputs using `.fill()` and checking for `type='date'` attributes, but the actual component renders these as `<p>` elements, so those assertions will definitely fail.\n\nThe real question is whether this counts as a directive violation or just a component-test mismatch. The tests do use data-testids correctly, so that part of the directive is satisfied. But the tests were written to verify user behavior against the current app implementation, and they don't match what's actually there — whether that's because the component changed after the tests were written or the tests were just written wrong, either way they won't pass.\n\nLooking at the actual violations though, the clearest issues are the missing `truncateAndSeed` calls in all six Property Detail test files, the missing `beforeEach` cleanup in files that modify database state like image-gallery.spec.ts, reviews-section.spec.ts, and host-info-card.spec.ts, and the destructive tests in image-gallery.spec.ts that aren't wrapped in `test.describe.serial`. The directive is explicit: any test file modifying database records needs a `beforeEach` cleanup that resets data through API calls. Now I'm identifying the specific violations in the writeApp.md and writeTests.md files. The app has issues with the Gallery not displaying captions, PropertyInfo missi